Generally, a garden shed under 2.5 metres high, sited behind the front wall of your house and covering less than half the garden, does not usually need a planning application.

A few things could change that:

- **Conservation area or listed building:** Different rules apply, so you may need to apply even for a small shed. If you tell me your address, I can check whether any constraints apply.
- **Position:** A shed in front of the house's front wall would not fall within the usual exemption.
- **Size and coverage:** If the shed would take up more than half the garden, it may need an application.

I can't give a formal planning opinion on your specific case. If you're unsure, the council's planning team can confirm whether your shed needs permission before you build it. If you share your address, I can check the constraints for it.
